  "title": "Chapter 46: Banking System in India",
  "order": 46,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k00jwbv",
      "content": "The banking system plays a crucial role in the economic development of a country. Banks mobilize savings from the public and provide loans for investment and development. The Indian banking system includes the Reserve Bank of India, commercial banks, regional rural banks and cooperative banks."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "RBI Established",
          "value": "1 April 1935",
          "icon": "calendar"
        },
        {
          "label": "RBI Nationalised",
          "value": "1949",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "First Nationalisation",
          "value": "1969 (14 Banks)",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "Primary Governing Act",
          "value": "RBI Act, 1934",
          "icon": "book"
        }
      ],
      "id": "4immjt4"
    },
    {
      "id": "0qa0qq2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Banking"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) serves as the supreme regulatory authority for the entire Indian monetary and banking structure.",
        "Commercial banks are divided into Public Sector, Private Sector, Foreign, and Regional Rural Banks (RRBs).",
        "Monetary Policy tools used by RBI to maintain liquidity and price stability include Quantitative (CRR, SLR, Repo Rate) and Qualitative controls.",
        "Primary bank account types include Savings Account, Current Account, Fixed Deposit (FD), and Recurring Deposit (RD).",
        "Modern digital banking operates seamlessly through transfer systems such as NEFT, RTGS, IMPS, and UPI."
      ],
      "id": "mus15tr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lyls9ne",
      "content": "• Banking refers to the business of accepting deposits and providing loans."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qln11ch",
      "content": "• Banks act as financial intermediaries between savers and borrowers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l96n188",
      "content": "• They facilitate economic development by promoting savings and investments."
    },
    {
