      "id": "ztg3w0b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Reserve Bank of India (RBI)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e00c1yp",
      "content": "The Reserve Bank of India is the central bank of the country. It was established in 1935 under the Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934."
    },
    {
      "id": "sm6db0x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Functions of RBI"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h1e66ft",
      "content": "• Issuer of currency notes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dz8zs0c",
      "content": "• Banker to the government."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tnhsjk8",
      "content": "• Banker’s bank."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "The Reserve Bank of India is the central bank of the country and regulates the entire banking system in India.",
      "id": "xlwhu0j"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xhu8vvk",
      "content": "• Controller of credit."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gmkk7g4",
      "content": "• Custodian of foreign exchange."
    },
    {
      "id": "nprbsvb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Commercial Banks"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gc8zlel",
      "content": "• Commercial banks accept deposits from the public."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ovi5gve",
      "content": "• They provide loans to individuals and businesses."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xwef4wg",
      "content": "• They facilitate trade and commerce."
    },
    {
